Negative edit_index can reach memory before msg[] array. read() uses msg_size[edit_index]-1 as size and msg[edit_index] as buffer.\"},{\"name\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1751\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"printf\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"_abort\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"view_index\",\"source\":\"scanf(%lld)\",\"type\":\"int64\"}],\"checks\":[\"view_index < cookie_num (signed comparison: cmp rdx,rax; jl) — NO lower bound check\"],\"memory_operations\":[{\"operation\":\"READ\",\"source\":\"msg[view_index]\",\"size\":8,\"destination\":\"printf format string argument (prints as string via %s)\"},{\"operation\":\"OUTPUT\",\"destination\":\"stdout\",\"size\":\"unbounded string\",\"notes\":\"printf prints msg[view_index] as string — potential info leak if pointing to arbitrary memory\"}],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"scanf\"],\"notes\":\"Index check is signed 'jl'. No lower bound check. Negative view_index can reach memory before msg[] array. printf uses %s format with msg[view_index] as argument — dereferences pointer and prints until null.\"},{\"name\":\"menu\",\"address\":\"0x17fd\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"puts\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"puts\"],\"notes\":\"Prints menu options.\"},{\"name\":\"main\",\"address\":\"0x187f\",\"callers\":[\"__libc_start_main\"],\"callees\":[\"init\",\"menu\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"eat_cookie\",\"create_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\",\"exit\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"menu_choice\",\"source\":\"scanf(%lld)\",\"type\":\"int64\"}],\"checks\":[\"switch on menu_choice 1-5\"],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"init\",\"menu\",\"scanf\",\"eat_cookie\",\"create_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\",\"exit\"],\"notes\":\"Main loop: calls init once, then loops menu+scanf+dispatch. Choice 1=eat, 2=create, 3=edit, 4=read, 5=exit.\"},{\"name\":\"_abort\",\"address\":\"0x11f5\",\"callers\":[\"init\",\"create_cookie\",\"eat_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\"],\"callees\":[\"printf\",\"exit\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"error_msg\",\"source\":\"rdi\",\"type\":\"char*\"}],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"exit\"],\"notes\":\"Prints error message and calls exit(1).\"}],\"attack_surfaces\":[{\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"input\":\"edit_index (scanf %lld, signed int64)\",\"operation\":\"WRITE to msg[edit_index] heap buffer with msg_size[edit_index]-1 bytes via read()\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"Attacker-controlled index with signed comparison (jl) and NO lower bound check. Negative index reaches memory before msg[] array (0x4060). msg_size[] at 0x4160 is 0x100 bytes after msg[], so negative indices could access msg_size entries or other globals. The read() writes to the pointer at msg[negative_index] with size from msg_size[negative_index]-1.\"},{\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"input\":\"view_index (scanf %lld, signed int64)\",\"operation\":\"READ and OUTPUT msg[view_index] via printf(%s)\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"Attacker-controlled index with signed comparison (jl) and NO lower bound check. Negative index reaches memory before msg[] array. printf(%s) dereferences the 8-byte value at msg[negative_index] as a pointer and prints string until null — potential arbitrary read / info leak.\"},{\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"input\":\"random_index (from /dev/urandom)\",\"operation\":\"FREE msg[random_index], then swap-remove msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[random_index]\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"After free, the freed pointer is swapped from msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[random_index]. The old slot msg[cookie_num-1] still holds the same pointer but cookie_num is decremented making it unreachable via normal index. However, if negative index or other OOB can reach the stale slot, UAF/double-free may be possible. The freed pointer is also printed via printf before free — info leak of heap address content.\"},{\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"input\":\"message_length (scanf %lld, max 256)\",\"operation\":\"ALLOC calloc(message_length, 1), WRITE read(0, buf, message_length)\",\"risk\":\"LOW\",\"reason\":\"Size is bounded to <= 256. calloc initializes to zero. Standard create operation. No obvious vulnerability in isolation.\"},{\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"input\":\"msg[view_index] pointer used as printf %s argument\",\"operation\":\"OUTPUT unbounded string from heap pointer\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"printf(%s) with heap pointer has no length limit. If the heap chunk content extends beyond allocated size (e.g., adjacent heap metadata or overlapping chunk), data beyond the message may be leaked.\"}],\"facts\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Binary is ELF64 amd64 PIE, dynamically linked, not stripped, compiled with GCC 10.2.0\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Security: Full RELRO, NX enabled, Canary found, PIE enabled, no FORTIFY, no CET (IBT/SHSTK)\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"libc is Ubuntu GLIBC 2.39-0ubuntu8.8 at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg array at 0x4060 (.bss), 32 elements x 8 bytes = 256 bytes, type char*[]\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg_size array at 0x4160 (.bss), 32 elements x 4 bytes = 128 bytes, type int32[]\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F006\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"cookie_num at 0x41e8 (.bss), 8 bytes, int64, initialized to 5 by init()\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F007\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"urandom at 0x41e0 (.bss), 8 bytes, FILE* handle for /dev/urandom opened in init()\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F008\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"init() creates 5 default cookies via strdup with sizes: msg[0]=0x50, msg[1]=0x30, msg[2]=0x18, msg[3]=0x38, msg[4]=0x40\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F009\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie checks cookie_num <= 0x1f (31) and message_length <= 0x100 (256), uses calloc(message_length, 1)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F010\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie uses fread from /dev/urandom to get random byte, computes random_index = byte % cookie_num (signed idiv), prints msg[idx] via printf before free, then swap-removes last element into freed slot\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F011\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie index check: 'cmp rdx, rax; jl 1692' where rax=cookie_num — signed less-than comparison, NO lower bound check on index\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F012\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie index check: 'cmp rdx, rax; jl 17bb' where rax=cookie_num — signed less-than comparison, NO lower bound check on index\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F013\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie read() call: read(0, msg[edit_index], msg_size[edit_index]-1) — both index used for pointer array and size array are attacker-controlled\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie printf call: printf('%s', msg[view_index]) — dereferences pointer at attacker-controlled index and prints as string\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F015\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"scanf format for all index inputs is %lld (signed int64), allowing negative values\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F016\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"GOT is Full RELRO (read-only after relocation), cannot be overwritten at runtime\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"alarm(60) set in init() — process will receive SIGALRM after 60 seconds\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg_size is located 0x100 bytes (256 bytes) after msg start: msg=0x4060, msg_size=0x4160\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F019\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg array has 32 slots (0x4060-0x415f), msg_size has 32 slots (0x4160-0x41df), urandom at 0x41e0, cookie_num at 0x41e8 — all in .bss contiguously\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F020\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"Negative index in edit_cookie/read_cookie: index=-1 accesses msg[-1] at 0x4058 (8 bytes before msg), which is in .bss between stderr(0x4040+8=0x4048) and msg(0x4060). Index=-4 accesses 0x4040 (stderr). The exact content at these locations needs runtime verification.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F021\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"msg_size[n] is at address 0x4160 + n*4. msg[n] is at 0x4060 + n*8. For negative index n, msg_size[n] and msg[n] access different offsets relative to their bases. The relationship between negative msg[] indices and msg_size[] entries requires careful calculation by S2.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F022\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie swap-remove: after free(msg[idx]), copies msg[cookie_num-1] -> msg[idx] and msg_size[cookie_num-1] -> msg_size[idx], then decrements cookie_num. The pointer at old msg[cookie_num-1] is NOT cleared — it remains as a stale/dangling pointer but is beyond the new cookie_num boundary.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F023\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"All index inputs use scanf(%lld) which parses signed 64-bit integers, and the comparison instruction 'jl' is signed jump-if-less — negative values pass the check\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Runtime content of .bss slots before msg[] (0x4048-0x405f) — these are accessed by negative indices\",\"reason\":\"Need runtime debugging to see actual values. stderr at 0x4040 is a FILE* pointer. The gap between 0x4048 and 0x4060 may contain padding or completed.0 at 0x4048.\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether negative index in edit_cookie can reach msg_size[] entries to control read size\",\"reason\":\"msg_size starts at 0x4160, msg starts at 0x4060. Negative indices go below 0x4060, away from msg_size. But very large positive indices within the signed range could potentially reach msg_size from msg[] perspective. S2 needs to calculate exact offset relationships.\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Whether the stale pointer in eat_cookie's swap-remove is reachable via negative index or other means\",\"reason\":\"The stale pointer is at msg[old_cookie_num-1] which is >= msg[5] initially. After eat_cookie, cookie_num decreases. The stale slot is at index = new_cookie_num which is within the valid range 0..new_cookie_num-1 only if another eat occurred. Need S2 to analyze reachability.\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Whether heap layout allows overlapping chunks or tcache poisoning via the eat_cookie free + swap pattern\",\"reason\":\"Depends on glibc 2.39 tcache behavior and allocation sizes. S2/S3 need to analyze heap state.\"},{\"id\":\"U005\",\"description\":\"Whether read_cookie printf(%s) can leak heap addresses or libc addresses from adjacent heap metadata\",\"reason\":\"Depends on heap layout and whether message buffers are adjacent to heap metadata containing pointers.\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, not stripped, GCC 10.2.0. Entry=0x1110. 11 program headers, 29 sections.\",\"sections\":\".text(0x1110,0x891,RX) .rodata(0x2000,0x266,R) .data(0x4000,0x10,RW) .bss(0x4020,0x1d0,RW) .got(0x3f58,0xa8,RW->R RELRO) .plt(0x1020,0xe0,RX) .init_array(0x3d58,0x8) .fini_array(0x3d60,0x8) .eh_frame(0x22e0,0x1e0,R)\",\"symbols\":\"main=0x187f init=0x1232 create_cookie=0x1399 eat_cookie=0x14e1 edit_cookie=0x1628 read_cookie=0x1751 menu=0x17fd _abort=0x11f5. Globals: msg=0x4060(256B,32xptr) msg_size=0x4160(128B,32xint) urandom=0x41e0(8B) cookie_num=0x41e8(8B) stdout=0x4020 stdin=0x4030 stderr=0x4040\",\"disassembly\":\"Key findings: edit_cookie/read_cookie use signed jl comparison with no lower bound. eat_cookie does printf before free then swap-remove without clearing stale pointer. create_cookie bounds size<=256. init creates 5 default cookies with strdup. scanf uses %lld (signed int64).\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":null,\"primitive_reports\":[],\"target_bug\":\"\",\"bug_reports\":[],\"impact_reports\":[],\"strategy_reports\":[],\"final_exploit_path\":\"\",\"final_report\":{}}",
