            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "In read_cookie, negative view_index causes msg[view_index] to read an 8-byte value from before the msg[] array. This value is then passed to printf(\"%s\") which dereferences it as a pointer and prints memory at that address until a null byte. If the OOB-read value happens to be a valid pointer (e.g., stderr/stdin/stdout FILE* at indices -4/-3/-2), memory at that pointer is leaked to stdout."
          },
