            "type": "OOB_WRITE",
            "status": "CANDIDATE",
            "reason": "In edit_cookie, negative edit_index causes both msg[edit_index] (buffer pointer) and msg_size[edit_index] (read size) to be read from out-of-bounds memory. The read() call then writes user-controlled data to the OOB-derived pointer with the OOB-derived size. If msg[edit_index] resolves to a valid writable address (e.g., a FILE* pointer like stderr at index -4), user data is written to that structure."
