          "type": "Logic Error",
          "description": "In eat_cookie, the swap-remove operation copies msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[idx] after freeing msg[idx], but does NOT clear msg[cookie_num-1]. When idx != cookie_num-1, this creates a double reference: both msg[idx] and msg[cookie_num-1] point to the same live heap chunk. After cookie_num is decremented, msg[old_cookie_num-1] is beyond the valid range. However, if the attacker subsequently creates enough cookies to push cookie_num back past old_cookie_num-1, the stale slot is overwritten before becoming accessible. The primary concern is the temporary window where two valid indices reference the same chunk — if one is freed via eat_cookie while the other remains accessible, a use-after-free condition occurs on the remaining reference."
